-// Windows has CreateFiber/SwitchToFiber. Elsewhere the same two-stack, one-at-
-// a-time model is a handful of ARM instructions: save the registers the AAPCS
-// says a callee must preserve (r4-r11, plus r12 to keep the frame 8-byte
-// aligned, lr as the resume address, and VFP d8-d15), store sp, load the other
-// stack's sp, restore, return into it. Exactly one fiber runs at any time, so
-// nothing races, and no OS threads or semaphores are involved.
+// The game runs on its own OS thread, and the two threads hand a single turn
+// back and forth: exactly one of them runs at any moment, so this has the same
+// semantics as the Windows fibers -- no races, game control flow untouched.
